## Forms, Resend, and Netlify

Implement real form submission through a Netlify Function. Never expose the Resend API key in browser code or use a `VITE_` variable for secrets.

- Read `RESEND_API_KEY`, `CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL`, and `CONTACT_TO_EMAIL` on the server.
- Use a verified sender address and the validated visitor email as `replyTo`.
- Validate all fields server-side as well as client-side; enforce field lengths, allowlisted inquiry/service values, and a reasonable request size.
- Render submitted content safely in emails and do not accept arbitrary recipients or sender addresses from the browser.
- Include a honeypot and server-enforced abuse protection suitable for Netlify. Do not rely on process-memory rate limiting across serverless invocations. If using a challenge provider or durable rate-limit service, document its setup and keep its secret server-side.
- Provide accessible idle, submitting, success, and failure states; preserve entered content after errors and prevent duplicate submissions while pending.
- Show success only after the server confirms the email provider accepted the request. Do not claim confirmed inbox delivery or a booked lesson.
- Do not log full form submissions or personal information unnecessarily.
- Return clear, non-sensitive errors and keep provider details out of browser responses.
- If email configuration is missing, fail gracefully with an editable unavailable message. Never simulate a successful submission.

Provide `.env.example` with placeholders and a README explaining local function development, Resend sender verification, environment setup, and Netlify deployment. Never commit real secrets. Include the Netlify SPA rewrite while preserving function routes.

## SEO optimization

Act as the website's SEO optimizer. Implement technical, on-page, and local SEO appropriate for a private piano and voice lesson business. Focus on useful content, crawlable pages, fast loading, and accurate business information. Do not promise rankings or invent business details to fill SEO fields.

- Give each page a unique, descriptive title, meta description, one clear primary heading, and a logical heading hierarchy. Store editable SEO copy in `data.js`.
- Organize content around relevant search intent, including piano lessons, voice lessons, the instructor's approach, and lesson inquiries. Add location-specific phrases only after the actual service area is supplied. Write naturally and avoid keyword stuffing, hidden keywords, or repetitive location pages.
- Pre-render the public React routes at build time, or use an equivalent Netlify-compatible rendering approach, so each route's meaningful content, title, metadata, and internal links appear in its initial HTML. Do not rely exclusively on client-side metadata changes. Keep this compatible with the required React stack and centralized `data.js` content.
- Use descriptive URLs, crawlable internal links, and relevant links between services, instructor information, Student Gallery, and Contact. Ensure direct visits and refreshes work for every public route.
- When the real production domain is configured, generate absolute canonical URLs, `sitemap.xml`, and `robots.txt` using that domain. Include only enabled, indexable public routes in the sitemap. Keep contact form query parameters out of canonical URLs. Never publish placeholder domains in metadata or sitemaps.
- Keep Netlify deploy previews and staging environments out of search results with environment-aware `noindex` directives or response headers. Check that the production environment is indexable once the domain and required content are ready. Document these settings.
- Generate JSON-LD structured data using an appropriate supported organization or local-business type and only verified facts. Keep its editable inputs in `data.js`, safely serialize it, and omit incomplete or unsupported properties. Do not add fabricated ratings, reviews, prices, opening hours, address details, or credentials. Do not promise rich-result eligibility.
- Keep the business name, address, and phone consistent wherever they appear after real details are supplied. Include directions and service-area information when available. Document Google Business Profile setup or updates as an owner task; do not claim an account has been created or verified.
- Add editable Open Graph and social sharing metadata, using an approved PNG sharing image. Supply accurate image alt text and descriptive filenames without keyword stuffing. Preserve the PNG-only image workflow while optimizing dimensions and loading behavior.
- Prioritize Core Web Vitals through appropriately sized images, reserved media dimensions, limited font files, deferred nonessential scripts, and lazy loading of the map and lightbox. Avoid shipping the interactive map on unrelated pages.
- Return a real HTTP 404 status for unknown routes in the deployed configuration while preserving valid React routes. Do not serve every unknown URL as an indexable successful page.
- Include placeholders for the production domain and optional Search Console verification value. Keep verification values configurable, and explain how the owner can submit the sitemap after deployment.
- Before launch, identify all unresolved placeholder content. Keep unfinished production pages out of search until their content is ready; do not silently index a placeholder-filled website.

Verify the generated HTML for each route, page titles, descriptions, canonicals, structured data, sitemap, robots directives, response statuses, and internal links. Run an appropriate performance and SEO audit, fix actionable implementation issues, and report any checks that require the real production domain or verified business information. Do not treat an audit score as a guarantee of rankings.

## Accessibility, responsiveness, and quality

- Use semantic HTML, a skip link, logical heading order, keyboard-accessible controls, and visible focus indicators.
- Provide accessible names for icon controls, useful alternative text for meaningful images, and empty alt text for decorative art.
- Associate form errors with fields and announce submission results appropriately.
- Ensure layouts work from small mobile screens through large desktop screens without horizontal overflow.
- Optimize and lazy-load gallery images, reserve image dimensions, and avoid unnecessary animation or heavy dependencies.
- Set editable page-specific titles and descriptions, social metadata, and a favicon. Use real canonical URLs only when configured.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences and ensure content remains available if animation is disabled.
- Include a friendly not-found route.

